"are indicated in the Army Lists section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attacks, hits & armour values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:126
msgid ""
"Some troops are better fighters than others, some are better trained, some "
"are more naturally violent and so on. So that we can represent these "
"different qualities in the warriors, monsters and weird creatures that are "
"found in the game, we assign three values to [.edit]#each stand#. These are "
"*Attacks*, *Hits* and *Armour*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "game-values/attacks-hits-armour.webp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Attacks |Hits |Armour\n"
"\n"
"|3       |3    |6+\n"
"|↙       |↓    | ↘\n"
"\n"
"<|This is the\n"
"basic number\n"
"of dice rolled\n"
"in combat –\n"
"the more dice,\n"
"the better at\n"
"fighting the\n"
"stand is and\n"
"the more hits\n"
"it will be able\n"
"to inflict.\n"
"^|The number of\n"
"hits the stand\n"
"can suffer\n"
"before it is\n"
"removed.\n"
">|The stand’s Armour\n"
"value indicates the\n"
"chance of nullifying\n"
"hits scored against\n"
"it. A value of 6+\n"
"indicates that a dice\n"
"roll of 6 is required\n"
"to nullify a hit, a\n"
"5+ that a 5 or 6 is\n"
"required and so on.\n"
"A value of 0 means\n"
"that the stand has\n"
"no armour.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shooting attacks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:174
msgid ""
"If troops carry bows or other missile weapons then they will have two Attack "
"dice values divided by a slash, for example 3/1 or 2/2. In this case, the "
"first number is always that used in hand-to-hand combat and the second value "
"is that used for shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command values"
msgstr ""

#.  Removed: your General and other important
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:191
msgid ""
"Command is another game value and a very important one too! Only characters "
"have a Command value and they use it when issuing orders. Values vary from "
"as low as 7 to as high as 10 but only the very best Generals have a value as "
"high as 10.  [.bo5a]#The higher the value, the more likely you are to be "
"able to order your troops to do what you want them to.# More about command "
"in due course."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "Points values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-values.adoc:203
msgid ""
"Each unit and character in the game is assigned a points value which "
"reflects its worth in the game – the more effective units and characters "
"having an appropriately higher value. Once the battle is finished, the total "
"points value of each side’s casualties determines who wins.  [."
"edit]#Otherwise,# points values don’t really affect the rules of play."
msgstr ""

